{"The canManage() method in GroupPermissionsV2 passes both AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW and AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE to hasPermission(), meaning it returns true if the user has EITHER scope. This allows users with only VIEW permission to perform management operations like creating top-level groups via GroupsResource.addTopLevelGroup(). The Javadoc and implementation both include VIEW, suggesting a copy-paste error from canView().": 0.9839375615119934, "The getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() method in V2 uses groupResource.getId() (the authorization resource's auto-generated UUID) when it should use groupResource.getName() (which contains the Keycloak group ID). The hasPermission() method looks up resources by name via resourceStore.findByName(server, groupId), but the passed value is a resource UUID, causing the lookup to fail. Additionally, granted.add(groupResource.getId()) adds resource UUIDs instead of group IDs, breaking user filtering by group membership since the returned IDs don't correspond to actual groups.": 0.9471362829208374}